(footprint "Rectangular_patch__2.45_GHz__probe-fed" (version 20221018) (generator pcb_antenna_designer)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Rectangular microstrip patch over a full ground plane, fed by a probe. The patch sizes itself from the design frequency F0, the substrate er (ER) and thickness (H) with the transmission-line model equations (Balanis): width W, effective er, fringe extension DL and resonant length L, shortened by LT (1 mm, from the simulation: the equations come out about 4 % low in frequency on FR-4). The probe offset XF from the centre sets the input impedance (more offset = higher; 8 mm gives 50 ohm). Patches are narrowband (a few percent on FR-4) and radiate broadside, away from the ground. After changing F0, also change the simulation frequency range.")
  (tags "antenna IFA MIFA RF")
